244
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:08,694
Is he making his own special effects?

245
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,029
Mummy with good sense
of showmanship.

246
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:15,951
This is stupid.

247
00:17:16,536 --> 00:17:18,829
Damn it. Jamie. I'm late.

248
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:21,832
You're good here with the mummy
and the crazy--?

249
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,625
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

250
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,508
[SIGHS]

251
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,721
Your loss, G-Man.

252
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:41,476
[FLAPPING]

253
00:17:48,359 --> 00:17:50,485
[IN DRACULA'S ACCENT]
Good evening.

254
00:17:59,579 --> 00:18:03,832
I have watched you for many nights
from afar.

255
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:07,627
My passion knows no bounds, Mina.

256
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:13,592
You are the reincarnation
of my beloved.

257
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:16,386
And l must have you.

258
00:18:17,138 --> 00:18:18,180
Aah!

259
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:20,182
[SPEAKS WlTH NO ACCENT]
Mary! Son of a--

260
00:18:22,602 --> 00:18:24,102
Jamie?

261
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:27,981
Son of a bitch.

262
00:18:28,149 --> 00:18:30,317
[WlTH ACCENT]
You should not use such language...

263
00:18:30,485 --> 00:18:32,778
...in the presence of my bride.

264
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:35,489
Okay.

265
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:37,324
Oh!

266
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:39,534
Haah!

267
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:43,997
[GRUNTS]

268
00:18:44,165 --> 00:18:45,207
Jamie, run!

269
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:51,463
You have no choice in the matter,
Mr. Harker. Mina is mine!

270
00:18:56,803 --> 00:18:58,303
[GRUNTS]

271
00:19:00,223 --> 00:19:01,640
[GROANS]

272
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:21,284
[ENGINE REVS]

273
00:19:29,377 --> 00:19:30,669
[HORN HONKS]

274
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:45,684
Hey.

275
00:19:45,852 --> 00:19:48,937
-You guys all right?
-Yeah, I think so.

276
00:19:49,105 --> 00:19:51,314
-And I think I know what's going on.
-Yeah?

277
00:19:51,482 --> 00:19:52,983
Part of it, at least.

278
00:19:56,279 --> 00:19:58,363
Uh.... The ear part?

279
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:00,991
Ripped it off Dracula's head. Touch it.

280
00:20:01,242 --> 00:20:02,742
[SCOFFS]

281
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:10,792
-Ugh.
-Feel familiar to you?

282
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:13,879
-Oh, man.
-Skin of a Shapeshifter.

283
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:16,298
Just like St. Louis
and just like Milwaukee.

284
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,301
Of course, this one's
all whole new buckets of crazy.

285
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:21,636
Oh, and...

286
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,473
...this. l pulled it off during the fight.

287
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:27,517
Look at the label on the ribbon.

288
00:20:30,688 --> 00:20:32,022
It's a costume rental.

289
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:34,983
All three monsters, the Dracula,
Wolf Man, the mummy...

290
00:20:35,151 --> 00:20:36,318
...all the same critter.

291
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:38,194
We need to catch this freak...

292
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,989
...before he Creature-From-the-Black-
Lagoons somebody.

293
00:20:41,157 --> 00:20:43,700
So you guys are like Mulder
and Scully or something?

294
00:20:43,868 --> 00:20:45,660
And The X Files are real?

295
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:49,706
Hmm. No, The X Files is a TV show.
This is real.

296
00:20:50,499 --> 00:20:51,833
Oh.

297
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:55,921
Okay, so the stagecraft, the costuming.

298
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:59,424
It's like he's trying to reenact
his favorite monster-movie moments...

299
00:20:59,592 --> 00:21:01,509
...right down to the bloody murders.

300
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,678
Wait a second. Who the hell is Mina?

301
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:06,181
SAM: Mina?
-Yeah, it's what he called Jamie.

302
00:21:06,349 --> 00:21:08,850
-He called me Mr. Harker.
-Jonathan Harker?

303
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:13,521
They're characters
from the movies and the novels.

304
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,941
Mina, Dracula's intended bride.

305
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:19,361
Harker, the fiance
that stands in the way.

306
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:22,572
Seems like he's fixating on you.
Like he sees you as his bride.

307
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:26,576
-Well, lucky me. Heh.
-But to fixate on you, my guess is...

308
00:21:26,744 --> 00:21:31,039
...that the shifter has to have seen you
before or been around you.

309
00:21:31,207 --> 00:21:33,875
Jamie, has anybody strange
come to town?

310
00:21:34,043 --> 00:21:36,378
Somebody that has taken
specific notice of you.

311
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:40,465
I don't know, Dean.
It's Oktoberfest. I'm a bartender.

312
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:44,636
There's lots of people. I--

313
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:48,556
-Wait a second, there is Ed.
-"Ed Brewer" Ed?

314
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:52,727
Yeah. He moved here
about a month ago.

315
00:21:52,895 --> 00:21:57,357
Lucy swears he has a crush on me.
He comes in almost every night.

316
00:21:58,109 --> 00:21:59,985
But l don't think
he's the type of guy--

317
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:03,071
-Where does Ed live?
-l don't know.

318
00:22:03,239 --> 00:22:05,115
But he works at the old movie theater.

319
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,575
I think he's the projectionist there.

320
00:22:08,911 --> 00:22:11,621
-Take care of Mina?
-Yup.

321
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:19,170
So monsters are real?

322
00:22:19,630 --> 00:22:23,299
-Some of them. Yeah.
-And this Shapeshifter...

323
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:26,428
...he could turn into different people?

324
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:29,431
Yeah. Except this one's
turning into...

325
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:33,435
...the great monsters of screenland,
which is a new one for me.

326
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:38,690
You're not really FBl, are you?

327
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:42,444
-Not so much.
-So...

328
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:45,530
...this is what you do?
You and your partner...

329
00:22:45,698 --> 00:22:48,283
...just tramp across the country
on your own dime...

330
00:22:48,451 --> 00:22:52,203
...until you find some
horrible nightmare to fight?

331
00:22:53,914 --> 00:22:55,957
Some people paint.

332
00:22:56,167 --> 00:22:58,001
Wow.

333
00:22:58,169 --> 00:22:59,294
What?

334
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:03,339
That must suck. l mean...

335
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:07,177
...you're giving up
your life for this terrible...

336
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:10,638
...l don't know, responsibility.

337
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:12,974
[CHUCKLES]

338
00:23:15,311 --> 00:23:19,147
Last few years,
I started thinking that way.

339
00:23:20,149 --> 00:23:24,736
And, you know, it started
sort of weighing on me.

340
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:28,073
Of course, that was before--

341
00:23:32,328 --> 00:23:33,703
[CHUCKLES]

342
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:42,337
A little while ago, I had this...

343
00:23:42,505 --> 00:23:45,423
...let's call it a near-death experience.

344
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,383
Very near.

345
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:52,972
And...

346
00:23:53,766 --> 00:23:57,352
...ahem, when l came to...

347
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:59,395
...things were different.

348
00:24:00,481 --> 00:24:03,441
My life's been different.

349
00:24:03,609 --> 00:24:07,195
I realized that l help people.

350
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:10,615
You know? Not just help them though,
I save them.

351
00:24:11,033 --> 00:24:14,536
And l gotta say, it's awesome.

352
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:19,249
It's kind of like a gift.

353
00:24:20,626 --> 00:24:23,378
Like a mission.

354
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:30,093
Kind of like a mission from God.

355
00:24:32,638 --> 00:24:37,058
So does that make you...

356
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:39,727
...some kind of monk or something?

357
00:24:40,938 --> 00:24:44,274
You know, celibate?

358
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:45,733
Man, l hope not.

359
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,777
[THUNDER CRASHES]

360
00:24:58,581 --> 00:25:00,081
[SWITCH CLlCKS]

361
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:04,586
Holy crap. Oh, my God, Jamie.

362
00:25:05,129 --> 00:25:08,923
Guys, l'm sorry. l thought
you guys were going out.

363
00:25:09,091 --> 00:25:11,467
Lucy, it's okay. Listen--

364
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:16,973
I came to borrow a bottle. l got
something going on back at my--

365
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:23,313
Anyway, you guys look really busy.
So l'm just gonna get out of your hair.

366
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:28,610
No, seriously, Lucy. lt's been
a crazy night. Stay for a drink.

367
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:31,613
Yeah, stay for a drink.

368
00:25:31,822 --> 00:25:33,198
[THUNDER CRASHES]

369
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:35,450
[ORGAN MUSlC PLAYlNG lNSIDE]

370
00:26:32,883 --> 00:26:35,009
[SWITCHES TO BOSSA NOVA]

371
00:26:40,933 --> 00:26:42,392
Whoa!

372
00:26:42,643 --> 00:26:44,227
You FBl man. What did l--?

373
00:26:44,395 --> 00:26:46,354
Shut up! Okay?
You know what you did.

374
00:26:46,522 --> 00:26:48,022
-What?
-l know what you are.

375
00:26:48,190 --> 00:26:50,525
I'm not anything.
I just like to play the Casio.

376
00:26:50,693 --> 00:26:53,528
-Had time to grow the ear back, huh?
-What? Ow!

377
00:26:53,696 --> 00:26:56,531
Ow! Ouch! Ouch!

378
00:26:58,367 --> 00:27:00,702
-lt's supposed to come off.
-No, it's not.

379
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:07,875
Oh, that sounds awful.
Jamie, honey, are you okay?

380
00:27:08,043 --> 00:27:11,713
I'm fine. He didn't even touch me.

381
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:15,383
Dean, he just, heh, flew right in
and fought him off.

382
00:27:15,551 --> 00:27:19,929
Well, l didn't actually fly. But l'm sure
it seemed that way at the time.

383
00:27:20,097 --> 00:27:23,182
It did. lt was really, really something.

384
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:27,103
-Jamie?
-Hmm.

385
00:27:27,271 --> 00:27:30,732
So, Dean, are you
like a black belt or what?

386
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:41,117
Well, l guess, they train you to fight
at the academy or whatever.

387
00:27:45,247 --> 00:27:47,790
JAMlE:
Dean! What are you doing?

388
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:50,418
[GRUNTS]

389
00:27:53,297 --> 00:27:54,422
It's you, isn't it?

390
00:28:03,974 --> 00:28:06,601
Oh! Damn it.

391
00:28:08,812 --> 00:28:11,439
What did you put in our drinks?

392
00:28:12,441 --> 00:28:16,027
It's all right, l'll skin you myself.

393
00:28:18,447 --> 00:28:20,531
[GLASS SHATTERlNG]

394
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:27,246
And scene.

395
00:28:32,669 --> 00:28:34,796
[ELECTRlClTY BUZZlNG]

396
00:28:53,023 --> 00:28:54,399
[GRUNTS]

397
00:29:00,489 --> 00:29:02,365
Oh, come on.

398
00:29:14,962 --> 00:29:17,964
She is beautiful, no?

399
00:29:18,674 --> 00:29:21,968
Bride Number 3 from the first film.

400
00:29:23,679 --> 00:29:27,473
She never got the acclaim
that she deserved...

401
00:29:29,059 --> 00:29:33,396
...which is why l chose her shape,
her form...

402
00:29:33,564 --> 00:29:36,858
...to move among
the mortals unnoticed...

403
00:29:37,025 --> 00:29:41,028
...to listen to the cricket songs
of the living.

404
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:47,577
That is when l discovered my bride
had been reborn...

405
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:49,036
...in this century.

406
00:29:49,204 --> 00:29:50,204
[SNlCKERS]

407
00:29:51,707 --> 00:29:56,878
I can't get over what a pumpkin-pie-eyed
crazy son of a bitch you really are.

408
00:29:57,045 --> 00:30:00,590
You're not Dracula.
You get that, right?

409
00:30:00,757 --> 00:30:02,592
Or even if you think
you are Dracula...

410
00:30:02,759 --> 00:30:04,719
...what the hell is up with the mummy?

411
00:30:07,431 --> 00:30:10,266
I am all monsters.

412
00:30:10,434 --> 00:30:13,603
Life ain't a movie, you sorry sack of--

413
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:19,150
-Aah.
-Life is small...

414
00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:23,279
...meager, messy.

415
00:30:24,072 --> 00:30:29,243
The movies are grand, simple, elegant.

416
00:30:29,411 --> 00:30:33,748
I have chosen elegance.

417
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:39,921
Yeah? Is "elegance" really the word
for what you did to Marissa?

418
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:43,925
Or Rick Deacon? Or any of the others?

419
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:49,347
But, of course, it is a monster movie
after all.

420
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:53,059
You do realize what happens
at the end of every monster movie?

421
00:30:53,268 --> 00:30:54,602
Ah.

422
00:30:54,937 --> 00:30:59,106
But this movie is mine.

423
00:31:00,108 --> 00:31:03,611
And in it, the monster wins.

424
00:31:03,779 --> 00:31:07,532
The monster gets the girl.

425
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:11,452
And the hero, he's...

426
00:31:11,620 --> 00:31:13,496
...electrocuted.

427
00:31:13,664 --> 00:31:15,289
[CHUCKLES]

428
00:31:15,457 --> 00:31:18,668
And tonight, Jonathan Harker...

429
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:23,172
...you will be my hero.

430
00:31:23,340 --> 00:31:26,133
Wait, wait, wait. Heh-heh.

431
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:37,645
[GRUNTS]

432
00:31:37,813 --> 00:31:40,398
[DOORBELL RlNGS]

433
00:31:41,692 --> 00:31:44,485
Please, excuse me.

434
00:31:49,616 --> 00:31:51,158
[CREAKING]

435
00:31:58,417 --> 00:32:01,168
[DOORBELL RlNGS]

436
00:32:05,507 --> 00:32:06,924
Good evening.

437
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,428
Uh....

438
00:32:10,637 --> 00:32:13,014
-Pizza delivery?
-Ah.

439
00:32:13,181 --> 00:32:16,559
You have brought a repast. Excellent.

440
00:32:17,394 --> 00:32:22,523
Continue to be of such service,
and your life will be spared.

441
00:32:23,859 --> 00:32:25,526
Uh-huh.

442
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:30,197
That'll be 1 5.50.

443
00:32:30,699 --> 00:32:32,408
-Tell me.
-Yeah?

444
00:32:32,576 --> 00:32:36,370
Is there garlic on this pizza?

445
00:32:38,415 --> 00:32:40,541
I don't know.

446
00:32:40,709 --> 00:32:42,960
-Did you order garlic?
-No.

447
00:32:43,170 --> 00:32:46,922
Then, no. Look, mister,
I got four other deliveries to make.

448
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:49,717
You wanna just pay me the money
so l can go?

449
00:32:49,885 --> 00:32:51,719
Of course. Yes.

450
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:55,056
But l have a coupon.

451
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:56,724
[DOOR CLOSES]

452
00:32:56,892 --> 00:32:58,225
[SIGHS]

453
00:33:02,773 --> 00:33:04,190
[PHONE BEEPS]

454
00:33:05,734 --> 00:33:08,903
Dean, hey listen. Ed is not our guy.

455
00:33:09,071 --> 00:33:12,406
I'm guessing you went home with Jamie,
so just give me a call, okay?

456
00:33:13,742 --> 00:33:15,117
[SIGHS]

457
00:33:18,622 --> 00:33:20,122
[THUNDER CRASHES]

458
00:33:23,919 --> 00:33:25,586
Lucy.

459
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:53,364
DRACULA:
You wake.

460
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:59,495
The gown, it suits your beauty.

461
00:33:59,663 --> 00:34:01,789
Please, put it on.

462
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:07,294
Where am l?
What have you done with Dean?

463
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:10,506
Harker is resting elsewhere.

464
00:34:10,674 --> 00:34:15,052
Please, put on the gown
and you may dine.

465
00:34:15,262 --> 00:34:17,555
We are having pizza.

466
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:24,478
What? What is wrong with you?

467
00:34:25,647 --> 00:34:28,315
You made up Lucy, right?

468
00:34:28,859 --> 00:34:30,526
Pretended to be my friend?

469
00:34:31,319 --> 00:34:33,988
I needed to know if you were the one.

470
00:34:34,156 --> 00:34:35,906
You could try talking to people.

471
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:38,868
-And instead you become this?
-The gown.

472
00:34:39,035 --> 00:34:42,872
I don't want to play
your stupid game. Okay? I just--

473
00:34:43,665 --> 00:34:44,832
I just want to go home.

474
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,501
[NO ACCENT]
Put on the gown!

475
00:34:55,010 --> 00:34:57,094
[TlCKlNG]

476
00:35:09,524 --> 00:35:10,524
[COCKS GUN]

477
00:35:24,539 --> 00:35:25,748
[THUNDER CRASHlNG]

478
00:35:34,049 --> 00:35:36,217
[NO ACCENT]
I-- l scared you.

479
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:41,138
You're the only one
I don't wanna scare.

480
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:53,984
I just love the movies.

481
00:35:55,237 --> 00:35:57,404
They aren't real.

482
00:35:57,572 --> 00:36:00,241
You can't make them real.

483
00:36:01,368 --> 00:36:06,372
Real is being born this way.

484
00:36:07,249 --> 00:36:09,083
Different.

485
00:36:09,251 --> 00:36:14,922
Real is having your dad
call you "monster."

486
00:36:15,382 --> 00:36:17,299
It's the first time you hear the word...

487
00:36:17,467 --> 00:36:20,970
...and he tries to beat you to death
with a shovel.

488
00:36:21,763 --> 00:36:26,267
Everywhere l ran, everywhere
I tried to hide, people found me.

489
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:29,019
Dragged me out, attacked me.

490
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:34,441
Called me "freak," called me "monster."

491
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:41,448
Tsk. Then l found them.

492
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:47,204
The great monsters.

493
00:36:47,414 --> 00:36:52,918
In their movies,
they were strong, they were feared.

494
00:36:54,421 --> 00:36:55,713
They were beautiful.

495
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:59,174
And now I am like them.

496
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:00,926
[SNlFFLING]

497
00:37:01,803 --> 00:37:03,846
Commanding.

498
00:37:06,141 --> 00:37:08,309
Terrifying.

499
00:37:09,561 --> 00:37:11,312
